-- title:
--   Step-15 chunk 16 of the fifteen-mod-16 branch: 2353 residue classes modulo $2^{24}$
-- statement:
--   Let $T(n)$ be the odd part of $3n+1$ (the platform's Syracuse map `syracuseStep`). This definition holds $R_{16}$, the explicit list of $2353$ distinct residue classes modulo $2^{24} = 16777216$ that carry a uniform fifteen-step Syracuse descent certificate on the fifteen-mod-16 branch.
--
--   Each listed residue satisfies $r \equiv 15 \pmod{16}$ and avoids every earlier exclusion list of the branch (moduli $128$, $256$, $1024$, $4096$, $8192$, $32768$, $65536$, $262144$ and $1048576$), as well as the ten already-certified modulus-$2^{23}$ step-14 chunks.
--
--   **Why a definition.** At this level the residual statement must carry sixteen chunk lists; publishing each list as a named `List ℕ` keeps every downstream statement flat instead of growing by a few hundred kilobytes, and lets the chunk theorem, its solution and the parent reduction all speak about the same literal.
--
--   **How the list was obtained.** For each class $r$ modulo $2^{23}$ surviving the branch's exclusions, and each of its two lifts modulo $2^{24}$, the checker `chk 14 r 24 r` was evaluated: fourteen exact rows $3 b_k + 1 = 2^{a_k} b_{k+1}$ with odd intermediate quotients, then a terminal row truncated to the remaining exponent budget, accepted when the truncated quotient lies below $r$. The 2353 residues listed are exactly those that pass.

